.TH ASK 1 "October 2026" "cli-ask 0.4.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ask \- lean terminal AI assistant with session-scoped context, inline prompt composer, code generation, and interactive chat
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.B ask
\fB--cg\fR | \fB--codegen\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.B ask
\fB--chatbot\fR | \fB-i\fR [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.B ask
\fB-o\fR | \fB--output\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.B ask
\fB-a\fR | \fB--append\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.B ask
[\fI--no-context\fR]
.br
.B ask
\fB--\fR \fIPROMPT\fR
.br
.I COMMAND
|
.B ask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ask
is a lightweight, zero-dependency command-line utility built in pure Go, designed for system administrators, DevOps engineers, and terminal users who want immediate, fluff-free AI answers without disrupting their shell workflow.
.PP
Unlike bloated TUI-based AI assistants, \fBask\fR acts as a native Unix filter: it executes directly from standard command pipelines, streams concise answers directly to standard output, and exits immediately. AI responses are formatted in clean, terminal-native plain text with ASCII underlines and readable indentation.
.PP
When invoked with no prompt arguments in an interactive terminal, \fBask\fR opens an inline multiline prompt composer directly within your active shell. Inside the composer, you can freely type or paste multiline text, edit lines using cross-line Backspace and Arrow keys, and insert blank lines without premature execution. The composer features an automatic sliding viewport (clamped to 5 lines maximum) to ensure your terminal output remains visible. Upon pressing \fBCtrl+S\fR (or \fBCtrl+Enter\fR), the composer closes, records your prompt into the terminal scrollback history, and streams the AI response to stdout. Pressing \fBCtrl+C\fR cancels and exits cleanly.
.PP
When invoked with \fB--chatbot\fR or \fB-i\fR, \fBask\fR launches an interactive continuous chat session. It supports multi-turn memory, mouse drag text selection, visual clipboard copying, on-the-fly model validation (\fB/model <name>\fR), and in-chat slash commands (\fB/clear\fR, \fB/model\fR, \fB/help\fR, \fB/exit\fR, \fB/q\fR). Exiting via \fB/exit\fR or \fBCtrl+C\fR cleanly restores your terminal screen and disables mouse tracking. Words without a leading slash are treated strictly as literal prompt text.
.PP
When invoked with \fB--cg\fR or \fB--codegen\fR, or when outputting to recognized code/script file extensions (\fI.sh\fR, \fI.py\fR, \fI.go\fR, \fI.rs\fR, \fI.yaml\fR, \fI.json\fR, etc.) or piping scripts, \fBask\fR automatically activates pure code generation mode. In this mode, conversational filler, markdown code fences, and title headers are strictly suppressed, producing 100% syntactically valid and runnable code starting directly from the first character or shebang.
.PP
Conversational context is automatically preserved and scoped to the parent shell process ID (PPID). Follow-up questions in the same terminal window retain knowledge of prior turns without cross-contaminating other shell tabs or tmux panes. Long conversations are automatically compacted to maintain responsiveness and avoid token window exhaustion.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-cg ", " \-\-cg ", " \-\-codegen
Enable pure code generation mode: outputs strictly raw, executable code or scripts without introductory titles, ASCII underlines, conversational filler, or markdown code fences.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the AI response directly to \fIFILE\fR (overwrites existing contents). Automatically enables pure code generation if \fIFILE\fR has a script/code extension.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-append " " \fIFILE\fR
Append the AI response directly to \fIFILE\fR (creates file if it does not exist).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-chatbot " [" \fIPROMPT\fR "]"
Start an interactive continuous chat session with conversation memory, mouse text selection, model switching, and quick clipboard copy. If an initial prompt is provided, it is submitted upon launch.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-clear
Clear the conversation history for the current terminal session.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-context
Execute the query as a standalone request without loading or updating the session history.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-self ", " \-\-update
Check for the latest release on GitHub and update the running binary in-place (and update the man page if installed).
.TP
.B \-\-
POSIX end-of-options delimiter. All following arguments are treated strictly as literal prompt text, ignoring any dashes or flags.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-key " " \fIAPI_KEY\fR
Save your OpenRouter API key to the user configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Set the default OpenRouter model slug (defaults to \fBnvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-config
Display the current configuration file path, active model, session identifier, and masked API key.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage help and exit.

.SH CHATBOT COMMANDS & SHORTCUTS
Within interactive chatbot mode (\fBask -i\fR), the following commands and shortcuts are available:
.TP
.BR /clear ", " /c
Clear conversation memory and reset session context.
.TP
.BR /model " [" \fIMODEL\fR "]"
Switch the active model for the chat session, or display current model if no argument is given. Entered model names are dynamically validated against OpenRouter models before switching; invalid names are rejected and the previous model is retained.
.TP
.B /help
Display available chatbot commands.
.TP
.BR /exit ", " /quit ", " /q
Exit chat mode and restore main terminal screen cleanly.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+S ", " Ctrl+Enter ", " Alt+Enter
Submit the multiline prompt to the AI. \fBCtrl+S\fR is the standard universal submit shortcut; \fBCtrl+Enter\fR and \fBAlt+Enter\fR are also supported.
.TP
.B Enter
Insert a newline within the prompt composer.
.TP
.B Mouse Drag
Highlight and select text within conversation history.
.TP
.BR y ", " Enter ", " Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy currently highlighted selection in history to system clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
If streaming, cancels active stream; otherwise displays exit confirmation prompt.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
If set, overrides the API key saved in the configuration file.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ask/config.json
User configuration containing API credentials and preferred model.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ask/sessions/session\-<PPID>.json
Session-scoped conversation history for the active terminal shell.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/ask.1
System manual page (or \fI~/.local/share/man/man1/ask.1\fR for user installations).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Quick command lookup:
ask "how to find listening ports in linux"
.TP
.B Code generation mode:
ask --cg "write a python function to compute sha256"
.TP
.B Direct file output:
ask -o deploy.sh "write a shell script to deploy container"
.TP
.B Follow-up in same terminal:
ask "filter only tcp ones"
.TP
.B Standard input piping:
git diff | ask "summarize these changes"
.TP
.B Inline multiline composer:
ask
.TP
.B Continuous chatbot mode:
ask -i
.TP
.B Clear active session:
ask --clear

